                                    "text": "param tuba_ring_blend 0.45 @min 0 @max 1",
                                    "varname": "tuba_ring_blend"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-33",
                                    "linecount": 64,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 579.0, 942.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nheterodyne_fof_resonator — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements Filterless Heterodyne & FOF (Fonction d'Onde Formantique) Resonant Synthesis from Lazzarini and Timoney (DAFx-12 Paper 58, Sections 2.1, 2.2, 3 & 3.1, Eq. 4–14, Fig. 2–4). Synthesizes sharp vocal/brass formant resonances and Casio CZ-style resonant waveforms without an IIR filter (eliminating filter instability and phase smearing). Synchronizes a periodic decaying exponential modulator `ephasor` M(n) = R^(n mod T0) — plus an optional FOF attack-skirt exponential Ma(n) - Mb(n) (Eq. 12) — to each period of the tuba's analytic phase, and multiplies it by two interpolated adjacent-harmonic cosine carriers (1-a)*cos(k*w0*n) + a*cos((k+1)*w0*n) (Eq. 8–10) for alias-free continuous formant sweeps.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba; in2 silent for 250 ms -> in1 is used for both sides)\n- in3: Tracked Fundamental Pitch f0 in Hz (from 00_tuba_freq_tracker; falls back to internal zero-crossing tracker if <= 0)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (sweeps formant_ratio twice per bar when sweep_depth > 0; an internal 0.5 Hz LFO takes over when in4 has not moved for 100 ms)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Heterodyne / FOF Resonant Output\n- Level: on the sousa_mic.aif take (-32 dB RMS in) about -33 dB RMS / -13 dBFS peak at the defaults (offline render of the real RNBO code).\n\nPARAMETERS (6)\n\n1. formant_ratio\n   - Range: 1.0 to 16.0 (Formant Center Frequency Ratio f_c / f_0, Default: 4.5)\n   - Taper: Continuous linear harmonic multiplier. Uses DAFx-12 Eq. 8–10 dual-carrier harmonic crossfading so fractional ratios never create phase-reset clicks.\n   - Function: Tunes the resonant formant center frequency to any harmonic or fractional multiple of the tuba's fundamental.\n\n2. resonance_q\n   - Range: 1.0 to 40.0 (Equivalent Resonator Quality Factor Q, Default: 12.0)\n   - Taper: Linear Q mapped via DAFx-12 Eq. 4 (R = exp(-pi * fc / (sr * Q))).\n   - Function: Controls the decay rate of the intra-period exponential envelope M(n), narrowing the formant bandwidth as Q increases.\n\n3. fof_attack_skirt\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = 2nd-Order All-Pole Impulse Decay Eq. 6, 1.0 = Full FOF Rounded Attack Skirt Ma(n) - Mb(n) Eq. 12)\n   - Taper: Linear blend.\n   - Function: Subtracts a faster-decaying secondary exponential at the start of each period (DAFx-12 Fig. 3), smoothing the grain onset and steepening the formant skirt roll-off like a true vocal FOF synthesizer.\n\n4. cz_window_mode\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = Exponential All-Pole / FOF Envelope, 1.0 = Casio CZ Sawtooth/Triangle Resonant Window Eq. 13–14)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade.\n   - Function: Morphs the intra-period formant envelope from physical exponential decay (0.0) to classic Casio CZ-101 linear sawtooth/triangle resonant windowing (1.0).\n\n5. sweep_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to +/- 1.2 Octaves of Counter-Phase Stereo Formant Sweep)\n   - Taper: Exponential octave sweep driven by the 1-bar phasor on in4.\n   - Function: Sweeps the Left and Right formant ratios in opposite directions for wide stereo vowel/talking-synth animation.\n\n6. tuba_ring_blend\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = Pure Phase-Locked FOF Formant Resynthesis, 1.0 = Heterodyne Formant Ring-Modulated Acoustic Tuba)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade.\n   - Function: Blends between pure FOF/CZ formant resynthesis and direct heterodyne formant excitation of the full acoustic tuba signal.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
